    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I find math challenging but fascinating. As a philosophy and chemistry student in Milan, I appreciate its logic but struggle with abstract concepts. I enjoy applying it to real-world problems, like analyzing chemical reactions, but feel overwhelmed by advanced topics like calculus. It’s a mix of curiosity and frustration.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Yes, sometimes. When I’m stuck on a problem or need to recall formulas quickly, anxiety creeps in. I’ve learned to take deep breaths and break problems into smaller steps. It’s not a constant worry, but during exams or complex assignments, I do feel nervous.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "I used a math app like Photomath for quick help with homework. It was useful for checking answers but sometimes gave incorrect solutions. I prefer human guidance for deeper understanding, so I’d avoid relying on AI for complex topics.",
