    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can personalize learning by adapting to individual paces, offering instant feedback on problems, and generating visual explanations. For example, they could break down complex topics like calculus into bite-sized lessons. This helps students grasp concepts without feeling overwhelmed, making math more accessible and engaging."
